// MC-smoke geometry: multiband lens+support MASS PROXY as a standalone,
// cosima-runnable setup. The Ge annulus is declared as a single-volume
// Scintillator (calorimeter) purely so cosima has a trigger; this proves the
// support-inclusive geometry loads and transports particles under Monte Carlo.
// Materials GeProxy/G10 (+ standard Vacuum/Aluminium) come from the project
// optics materials file, exactly as the real optics near-field model uses them.

Name multiband_mc_smoke
Version 1

SurroundingSphere 18 0 0 0 18

Include /home/ubuntu/TES_511_Balloon/add_mass/TES_511_Balloon_nearfield_mass_proxy_v2/optics/Materials_OpticsNearfield_v2.geo

Volume WorldVolume
WorldVolume.Material Vacuum
WorldVolume.Visibility 0
WorldVolume.Shape BRIK 100.0 100.0 100.0
WorldVolume.Mother 0

Volume InstrumentFrame
InstrumentFrame.Material Vacuum
InstrumentFrame.Visibility 0
InstrumentFrame.Shape BRIK 60.0 60.0 60.0
InstrumentFrame.Position 0 0 0
InstrumentFrame.Mother WorldVolume

Include /home/ubuntu/opticsim/opticsim_full/designs/f10m_multiband_20260701/OpticsMultiband_GeAndSupport_f10m.geo

//------------------------------------------------------------
// Detector: make the Ge mass-proxy annulus a simple calorimeter.

Scintillator GeDetector
GeDetector.DetectorVolume  MB_GeActiveMass_EqualVolumeAnnulus
GeDetector.SensitiveVolume MB_GeActiveMass_EqualVolumeAnnulus
GeDetector.NoiseThreshold   0.000001
GeDetector.TriggerThreshold 0.000001
GeDetector.EnergyResolution ideal
GeDetector.FailureRate 0.0

Trigger TN01
TN01.Veto false
TN01.TriggerByChannel true
TN01.Detector GeDetector 1
